    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and all four ops requirements work. `pytest -q` passes, though the repo's only test checks the logger's name.\n\nTo check the rest, I ran a stub transport where the first request fails with a 500 and the retry succeeds:\n- **Retry logging:** `app.http INFO GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models` was logged twice, once for the first request and once for the retry.\n- **Timeouts:** each request went out with connect 5s and read/write/pool 30s.\n- **Retries:** the client reports `max_retries=2`.\n- **Transport:** the stub was actually used, since it received both requests.\n\n**How it works:**\n- It builds the HTTP client with the SDK's own `DefaultHttpxClient` rather than a plain `httpx.Client`, so it keeps the SDK's connection limits and redirect behaviour.\n- A request event hook on that client does the logging. Because it runs on every request the client sends, the SDK's retries get logged too.\n- The timeout is set on both the HTTP client and the `OpenAI` client, because the SDK applies its own timeout to each request.\n- If `transport` is `None`, the HTTP client uses its normal default transport.\n\nNo dependencies were added. `httpx` was already installed as a dependency of `openai`.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** I couldn't delete my temporary check script `_smoke.py` in the project root because the removal needed your approval. Please delete it, or tell me to and I will."
